    "selection_rule": "Per (grid, bytes per CTA) retain the larger achieved fraction across the two independent clock-gated captures on the owned device, and publish only cells whose trial spread stayed inside ten percent on both; the rest are recorded as excluded in the captures. The larger fraction is the conservative choice because a completion floor divides by it. A lookup must not interpolate below the published points: it takes the measured grid and length at or above the requested ones, which keeps the fraction an upper envelope and the floor a lower bound.",
    "capacity_note": "The denominator is the envelope of the H200 saturated read capacity from dram_read_capacity_protocol_sm90.json (dram_read_bw.cu, 4.5126e+12 B/s) and this probe's own long-stream asymptote: single-CTA-per-SM streams at 112-132 CTAs exceed dram_read_bw by up to about 2.4 percent, so the larger measured rate is the capacity and every fraction is <= 1.",
    "saturated_probe_capacity_bytes_per_s": 4512600000000.0
  },
